<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>thermal_cam</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>Leoncio Hermosillo</name>
    <email>lhermosillo@pheratech.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>
    Radiometric LWIR camera, sized and configured after a FLIR Boson 320 (320x256,
    50 deg HFOV). Publishes 16-bit mono (L_INT16) on the entity-scoped default topic.
    Decode with kelvin = pixel * 0.01; saturates at 655.35 K.

    Two things that are not obvious and are easy to get wrong - both measured, see
    model.sdf for the numbers:
      - The 0.01 resolution is NOT the accuracy. Heat sources quantise to 2.57 K steps
        upstream of the 16-bit output; only ambient shading is truly fine-grained.
      - Thermal sensors ignore visibility_mask/visibility_flags, so the fork's
        hide-the-airframe trick does not work on this camera.

    Needs heat sources to show anything: gz gives every visual WITHOUT a
    gz-sim-thermal-system plugin the world's atmosphere temperature, so an unmodified
    PX4 world renders as a near-flat field around 288 K.
  </description>
</model>
